Likewise in the month of Āśvayuja, fasting and self-controlled,
he should bathe with cow dung on the ninth day and perform worship with lotuses;
he should offer incense of sal resin and a food offering of honeyed sweetmeats.

incense is bilva resin, and the food offering is boiled rice with honey;
having offered red rice, it is declared to be the priestly gift,
and the wise should say, 'Homage, may Śarva be pleased!'

He should present boiled rice with molasses together with clarified butter in a copper vessel as an offering;
and, O sage, he should gratify [a Brahmin] with the priestly gift together with the offering,
and a pair of garments for the twice-born, uttering the name of Rudra.
